meta {
  name: Share Bill All
  type: http
  seq: 32
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/share-bill-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "recipientType": "PATIENT",
    "email": "patient@example.com",
    "whatsapp": "919999999999"
  }
}

docs {
  "Share Bill All" from the Billings page: in one call, send the order's bill PDF
  (the tenant's `accounts_biling` template) to the chosen recipient over Email +
  WhatsApp AND raise the in-app (IAM) notification.

  ## Body
  - `recipientType` (required) — `PATIENT` or `PANEL` (Accounts Person) for the
    Email/WhatsApp recipient.
  - `email` / `whatsapp` (optional) — override the auto-filled recipient for that
    channel (blank = the recipient's stored contact).

  ## IAM recipients
  The in-app notification targets the **order creator** and any **referral party**
  that resolves to a person (the internal referral's linked employee) — NOT the
  patient. Referral panels / external referrals are B2B contacts with no in-app
  user, so they receive the bill over Email/WhatsApp instead.

  Each channel is attempted independently and never aborts the others:
  - QUEUED  — handed to the queue (Email/WhatsApp) or created in-app (IAM).
  - SKIPPED — no activated template for the channel, or no recipient on file.
  - FAILED  — an error (e.g. WhatsApp template missing its approved id).

  Returns `{ orderId, results: [{ channel, status, reason?, logId? }] }`.
  The bill PDF is rendered at most once and reused across Email/WhatsApp.

  Prereqs: activated `order_bill_as_attachment` messaging templates (Email /
  WhatsApp / IAM as desired) + an active `accounts_biling` PDF template.
}
